     There are no optimizations or loops to mark


    1.          SUBROUTINE XERROR(MESSG,NMESSG,NERR,LEVEL)
    2.    C***BEGIN PROLOGUE  XERROR
    3.    C***DATE WRITTEN   790801   (YYMMDD)
    4.    C***REVISION DATE  820801   (YYMMDD)
    5.    C***CATEGORY NO.  R3C
    6.    C***KEYWORDS  ERROR,XERROR PACKAGE
    7.    C***AUTHOR  JONES, R. E., (SNLA)
    8.    C***PURPOSE  Processes an error (diagnostic) message.
    9.    C***DESCRIPTION
   10.    C     Abstract
   11.    C        XERROR processes a diagnostic message, in a manner
   12.    C        determined by the value of LEVEL and the current value
   13.    C        of the library error control flag, KONTRL.
   14.    C        (See subroutine XSETF for details.)
   15.    C
   16.    C     Description of Parameters
   17.    C      --Input--
   18.    C        MESSG - the Hollerith message to be processed, containing
   19.    C                no more than 72 characters.
   20.    C        NMESSG- the actual number of characters in MESSG.
   21.    C        NERR  - the error number associated with this message.
   22.    C                NERR must not be zero.
   23.    C        LEVEL - error category.
   24.    C                =2 means this is an unconditionally fatal error.
   25.    C                =1 means this is a recoverable error.  (I.e., it is
   26.    C                   non-fatal if XSETF has been appropriately called.)
   27.    C                =0 means this is a warning message only.
   28.    C                =-1 means this is a warning message which is to be
   29.    C                   printed at most once, regardless of how many
   30.    C                   times this call is executed.
   31.    C
   32.    C     Examples
   33.    C        CALL XERROR('SMOOTH -- NUM WAS ZERO.',23,1,2)
   34.    C        CALL XERROR('INTEG  -- LESS THAN FULL ACCURACY ACHIEVED.',
   35.    C                    43,2,1)
   36.    C        CALL XERROR('ROOTER -- ACTUAL ZERO OF F FOUND BEFORE INTERVAL F
   37.    C    1ULLY COLLAPSED.',65,3,0)
   38.    C        CALL XERROR('EXP    -- UNDERFLOWS BEING SET TO ZERO.',39,1,-1)
   39.    C
   40.    C     Latest revision ---  19 MAR 1980
   41.    C     Written by Ron Jones, with SLATEC Common Math Library Subcommittee
   42.    C***REFERENCES  JONES R.E., KAHANER D.K., "XERROR, THE SLATEC ERROR-
   43.    C                 HANDLING PACKAGE", SAND82-0800, SANDIA LABORATORIES,
   44.    C                 1982.
   45.    C***ROUTINES CALLED  XERRWV
   46.    C***END PROLOGUE  XERROR
   47.          CHARACTER*(*) MESSG
   48.    C***FIRST EXECUTABLE STATEMENT  XERROR
   49.          CALL XERRWV(MESSG,NMESSG,NERR,LEVEL,0,0,0,0,0.,0.)
   50.          RETURN
   51.          END

